Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Quality=20=C2=B7=20source=20runs=20on=20ubuntu-?=
 =?UTF-8?q?24.04=20instead=20of=20xcode-27=20(swift-institute/institute#28?=
 =?UTF-8?q?7,=20step=202),=20and=20the=20planner=20pin=20moves=20to=20the?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20first=20planner=20that=20can=20lint=20there.?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The lint reads source text and nothing in it depends on the platform. Since institute d1f2ca2 its three tools are pinned by digest for linux-x86_64 as they are for macOS: swift-format from swift.org's swift-6.4.2-RELEASE toolchain for ubuntu24.04, SwiftLint 0.65.1's Linux build, and the Linux build of the pinned linter runner. So the job needs no macOS runner, and the same command runs wherever the code is written.

The job names the image and the Swift release exactly. The pinned swift-format is the one in the ubuntu24.04 toolchain of 6.4.2; ubuntu-latest or the 6.4 line would one day install another build, and the planner refuses a swift-format that does not hash to its pin. institute-ci installs the toolchain first on PATH, where the planner looks for it, and puts its runtime on the loader path. --xcode-application goes: it is accepted on macOS only. Every rule, limit and digest check is unchanged.

The pin moves with the workflow in one commit: the planner at the old pin has no Linux tools and requires --xcode-application, and the new one refuses that option on Linux.
---
 .github/workflows/swift-ci.yml | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 .institute-ci-pin              |  2 +-
 .institute-ci-planner          |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/swift-ci.yml b/.github/workflows/swift-ci.yml
index 6ffb7e5..b218e04 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/swift-ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/swift-ci.yml
@@ -665,7 +665,13 @@ jobs:
     name: Quality · source
     needs: plan
     if: ${{ !github.event.repository.private && !cancelled() && contains(format(',{0},', needs.plan.outputs.legs), ',source,') }}
-    runs-on: xcode-27
+    # Linux, since swift-institute/institute#287: the lint reads source text
+    # and its three tools are pinned by digest for linux-x86_64 as they are
+    # for macOS, so it needs no macOS runner. The image is named exactly,
+    # not ubuntu-latest: Institute.Source.Policy pins the swift-format of
+    # swift.org's ubuntu24.04 toolchain, and another image would install
+    # another build of it, which the planner refuses.
+    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
     timeout-minutes: ${{ fromJSON(needs.plan.outputs.timeout-minutes) }}
     permissions:
       contents: read
@@ -677,13 +683,19 @@ jobs:
         with:
           repository: ${{ needs.plan.outputs.subject-repository }}
           sha: ${{ needs.plan.outputs.subject-sha }}
+      # The exact release, not the 6.4 line: this toolchain's swift-format is
+      # the lint's engine, pinned by digest in Institute.Source.Policy. The
+      # action puts the toolchain first on PATH, where the planner looks for
+      # swift-format, and its runtime on the loader path. When the policy's
+      # pin moves to another release, this line moves with it.
       - id: institute-ci
         uses: swift-institute/.github/.github/actions/institute-ci@255dd9b55d9eef5b8cc1c9c2058e347fec0dd57f
+        with:
+          swift-version: '6.4.2'
       - name: Measure source
         shell: bash
         env:
           BINARY: ${{ steps.institute-ci.outputs.binary }}
-          DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH: ${{ steps.institute-ci.outputs.runtime-library-path }}
         # The JSON report on stdout is also kept as the `quality-report`
         # artifact: the log copy is subject to GitHub's secret masking, which
         # rewrites substrings to `***` and leaves the JSON unparsable.
@@ -695,7 +707,6 @@ jobs:
             --repository "${{ needs.plan.outputs.subject-repository }}" \
             --revision "${{ needs.plan.outputs.subject-sha }}" \
             --root "$GITHUB_WORKSPACE" \
-            --xcode-application "/Applications/Xcode_${XCODE_VERSION}.app" \
             | tee "$RUNNER_TEMP/quality/report.json"
       - name: Keep the Quality report
         if: always()
diff --git a/.institute-ci-pin b/.institute-ci-pin
